KZ2 patch 6043: the SPU runtime's condition variables on ps3_evcv (patch 6041) instead of the Win32
CONDITION_VARIABLE: the blocking channel read (spu_ch_wait, 10 ms slices while an SPU waits on its mailbox, signal
notification or event channel; woken by spu_ch_wake on every producer write), the SPURS task WAIT_SIGNAL park
(spu_workload.c, 1 s slices) and the async SPU task pool's idle wait (spu_async_pool.h, patch 6031, timed). Under Wine
these waited in ntdll's RtlWaitOnAddress, whose futex queue corrupts itself when a timeout meets a wake (patch 6041's
header); the channel wait is the busiest timed wait left after patch 7007. Same API and behaviour; the pthread
branches are unchanged.

--- a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #endif
 #include <time.h>
 #include "../platform/win32_compat.h"
+#include "../platform/ps3_evcv.h"   /* patch 6043: the channel-stall wait on ps3_evcv, no ntdll futex queue */
 #include "ps3emu/log_first.h"
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
@@ -1270,7 +1271,7 @@
 void spu_ch_wake(spu_context* ctx)
 {
     if (!ctx) return;
-    WakeAllConditionVariable((CONDITION_VARIABLE*)&ctx->ch_wait_cv);
+    ps3_evcv_wake_all((ps3_evcv*)&ctx->ch_wait_cv);   /* patch 6043 */
 }
 
